within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.V_Various.V08A_XRayContrastMediaIodinated.V08AB02_Iohexol;
model Iohexol "Iohexol — default model: Iohexol_Taubert2018_reference"
  extends Iohexol_Taubert2018_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of iohexol: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.V_Various.V08A_XRayContrastMediaIodinated.V08AB02_Iohexol.Iohexol_Taubert2018_reference\">Iohexol_Taubert2018_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of iohexol in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Iohexol_Hooper2025_final</code></li><li><code>Iohexol_Hooper2025_stoch_approx</code></li><li><code>Iohexol_Taubert2018_reference</code></li><li><code>Iohexol_sberg2020_mean</code></li><li><code>Iohexol_sberg2020_median</code></li></ul><h4>About iohexol</h4><p>Iohexol is an iodinated X-ray contrast agent used to visualise tissues and blood vessels during imaging procedures. It is widely used in medical imaging and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q410683\">Wikidata Q410683</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Iohexol\">Iohexol</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Iohexol;
